[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":147},["ShallowReactive",2],{"content-query-cAIsVzD59U":3},{"_path":4,"_dir":5,"_draft":6,"_partial":6,"_locale":7,"title":8,"description":9,"body":10,"_type":141,"_id":142,"_source":143,"_file":144,"_stem":145,"_extension":146},"/en/about-amber","en",false,"","About Amber","Baltic amber holds many secrets. Formed by nature, this fossilised resin evokes positive energy, serves as a good luck charm, and recalls seaside memories. Often called the Gold of the Baltic and the Living Stone, it captivates with its timeless allure.",{"type":11,"children":12,"toc":138},"root",[13,43,52,64,81,86,93,105,112],{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":16,"children":17},"element","p",{},[18,21,27,29,34,36,41],{"type":19,"value":20},"text","Baltic amber holds many secrets. ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":23,"children":24},"strong",{},[25],{"type":19,"value":26},"Formed by nature",{"type":19,"value":28},", this fossilised resin evokes positive energy, serves as a good luck charm, and recalls seaside memories. Often called the ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":30,"children":31},{},[32],{"type":19,"value":33},"Gold of the Baltic",{"type":19,"value":35}," and ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":37,"children":38},{},[39],{"type":19,"value":40},"the Living Stone",{"type":19,"value":42},", it captivates with its timeless allure.",{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":44,"children":45},{},[46],{"type":14,"tag":47,"props":48,"children":51},"img",{"alt":49,"src":50},"image alt text","/img/brylki/info/bursztyn.jpg",[],{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":53,"children":54},{},[55,57,62],{"type":19,"value":56},"The way people have different skin colours, amber comes in different colours too, and ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":58,"children":59},{},[60],{"type":19,"value":61},"no two pieces are identical",{"type":19,"value":63},". Its colours result from changes in the resin and conditions underground over millions of years. Baltic amber has a darker surface skin than the interior. Exploring the interior color is worthwhile.",{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":65,"children":66},{},[67,71],{"type":14,"tag":47,"props":68,"children":70},{"alt":49,"src":69},"/img/brylki/info/13.jpg",[],{"type":14,"tag":72,"props":73,"children":78},"span",{"className":74},[75,76,77],"text-subtitle2","text-caption","self-center",[79],{"type":19,"value":80},"Birds, sculpture | Przemysław Kuś",{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":82,"children":83},{},[84],{"type":19,"value":85},"People have named and described over 100 colour varieties of Baltic amber!, with yellow being the most common, symbolizing the sun.",{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":87,"children":88},{},[89],{"type":14,"tag":47,"props":90,"children":92},{"alt":49,"src":91},"/img/brylki/info/bursztyny.jpg",[],{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":94,"children":95},{},[96,98,103],{"type":19,"value":97},"Amber often features patterns of multiple colours, and its hues darken over time, becoming noble - ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":99,"children":100},{},[101],{"type":19,"value":102},"more intense and saturated",{"type":19,"value":104},".",{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":106,"children":107},{},[108],{"type":14,"tag":47,"props":109,"children":111},{"alt":49,"src":110},"/img/brylki/info/brylki.jpg",[],{"type":14,"tag":15,"props":113,"children":114},{},[115,117,122,124,129,131,136],{"type":19,"value":116},"It can be ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":118,"children":119},{},[120],{"type":19,"value":121},"transparent",{"type":19,"value":123},", ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":125,"children":126},{},[127],{"type":19,"value":128},"translucent",{"type":19,"value":130},", or ",{"type":14,"tag":22,"props":132,"children":133},{},[134],{"type":19,"value":135},"opaque",{"type":19,"value":137},". White amber gets its colour from microscopic gas bubbles trapped during hardening—the more bubbles, the lighter and less transparent it becomes.",{"title":7,"searchDepth":139,"depth":139,"links":140},2,[],"markdown","content:en:about-amber.md","content","en/about-amber.md","en/about-amber","md",1739449681403]